mscms: answer the Windows Color System queries (WcsGetDefaultColorProfile, WcsEnumColorProfiles, ...) and the color-directory/standard-profile size queries as Windows 11 does

What was seen (app batch 1, the request: "Let's start with these. I can make the accounts. Once we get these solid, we can
move onto the rest."): Affinity 3.3.3 (Canva) logs at every start, once per monitor, "WcsGetUsePerUserProfiles error 120 -
Call not implemented", "GetStandardColorSpaceProfile error 122 - Insufficient buffer", "WcsOpenColorProfile error 3 -
Path not found", then "WcsEnumColorProfilesSize error 120" for both scopes (8 ColourProfileManager errors): it cannot list
the installed color profiles, cannot pick up a display profile, and opens "" as the display's profile.

Mechanism (SOLID: +mscms trace, and the disassembly of Serif.Interop.Persona.dll's ColourProfileManager): per monitor
(device = the monitor's DeviceKey "\Registry\Machine\System\CurrentControlSet\Control\Class\{4D36E96E-...}\000N") it calls
WcsGetUsePerUserProfiles(dev, CLASS_MONITOR), then WcsGetDefaultColorProfileSize/WcsGetDefaultColorProfile(scope, dev,
CPT_ICC, CPST_RGB_WORKING_SPACE). A failure there is its expected path (not logged): it falls back to
GetStandardColorSpaceProfileW(NULL, LCS_sRGB, NULL, &size) with size = 0, IGNORES the return value and uses the size the
call wrote (size == 0: logs the error and returns ""), makes a string of size/2 - 1 characters, calls again with it, takes
PathFindFileNameW of the result and opens it with WcsOpenColorProfileW. An ICC profile ('acsp') is used directly; only a
WCS device model profile ('cdmp', CMM 'wcs1') goes through WcsCreateIccProfile(h, WCS_ICCONLY). Then
WcsGetDefaultRenderingIntent and WcsEnumColorProfilesSize/WcsEnumColorProfiles for SYSTEM_WIDE and CURRENT_USER. Wine
answered ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED to every Wcs* query (WcsEnumColorProfiles and WcsCreateIccProfile were `stub` entries:
a call raised), and its GetStandardColorSpaceProfileW size query left the size untouched, so the fallback opened "".

Windows (the Windows 11 measurement, build 26200, a display with no associated profile; probes wcsprobe in the affcolor
lab folder and wcsprobe2 in the affcolor2 lab folder):
- GetStandardColorSpaceProfileW(LCS_sRGB or LCS_WINDOWS_COLOR_SPACE): a NULL or short buffer fails with
  ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER and writes the size, counting the terminator; id 0 fails with ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND. Affinity's
  fallback, replayed step by step, opens the sRGB ICC profile. GetColorDirectoryW's NULL-buffer query: the same error, the
  size counting the terminator.
- WcsGetUsePerUserProfiles: TRUE, use FALSE, for a monitor key, its adapter name, its device ID or "" with CLASS_MONITOR
  and for CLASS_SCANNER on the monitor key; TRUE for CLASS_PRINTER there; ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER for class 0 or 'abcd'
  and for a NULL name.
- WcsGetDefaultColorProfile(Size): ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND for the display (CPST_RGB_WORKING_SPACE, CPST_NONE, CPST_PERCEPTUAL
  per user, scope 5, subtype 99, CPT_DMP/CAMP/GMMP), for its adapter name, device ID or "" (CPST_RGB_WORKING_SPACE), and
  for a NULL device with CPST_RGB_WORKING_SPACE;
  ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER for type 9, a NULL device with CPT_DMP, CPST_NONE or CPST_PERCEPTUAL, a NULL buffer or a NULL
  size pointer. A NULL device with CPT_CAMP / CPT_GMMP names Windows' shipped D65.camp / Photo.gmmp.
- WcsGetDefaultRenderingIntent: TRUE, INTENT_PERCEPTUAL for both scopes.
- WcsEnumColorProfiles: the same MULTI_SZ of file names for CURRENT_USER as for SYSTEM_WIDE (there 30 ICC + 8 WCS
  profiles; 17 for ET_DEVICECLASS / ET_CLASS 'mntr' and ET_DATACOLORSPACE RGB); ET_DEVICENAME of the display: none, both
  scopes; a buffer 2 bytes short: ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER; a bad version, size, scope or a NULL record:
  ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER.
- GetColorProfileFromHandle's NULL-buffer size query: ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER.
- WcsCreateIccProfile: NULL, ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER for an ICC handle (WcsOpenColorProfileW or OpenColorProfileW, either
  option) and for NULL; it succeeds only for a WCS profile handle.

Fix (dlls/mscms/profile.c, mscms.spec), on the store Wine already has -- the color directory (installed profiles) and the
per-class associations AssociateColorProfileWithDevice writes under HKLM\...\ICM\<class>, which gdi32's GetICMProfile
reads for a display:
- GetStandardColorSpaceProfileW and GetColorDirectoryW: the size counts the terminator (the old count let a buffer of
  exactly that size be overrun by one character); a NULL or short buffer fails with ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER and gets
  the size. OpenColorProfileW's own color-directory size query follows (it relied on ERROR_MORE_DATA).
- WcsGetDefaultColorProfile(Size): unknown type, or a NULL device with CPT_DMP or an ICC subtype other than the working
  spaces: ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER. A device's CPT_ICC default = its class's first association (device class from the
  name: monitor DeviceKey / MONITOR\ device ID / \\.\DISPLAY, printer, image class GUIDs), scope and subtype not checked;
  everything else ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND (Wine records no device-independent defaults: WcsSetDefaultColorProfile is a stub;
  no WCS-format profiles). Size in bytes with the terminator; name only, which OpenColorProfile resolves in the color
  directory.
- WcsEnumColorProfiles(Size): every installed .icm/.icc whose header matches the ENUMTYPE (ET_DEVICECLASS compared with the
  profile class), with ET_DEVICENAME the device class's associations; the same list for both scopes. Exported for real.
- WcsGetUsePerUserProfiles: FALSE (Wine keeps no per-user association lists); a NULL name/pointer or a class other than
  monitor/printer/scanner is ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER.
- WcsGetDefaultRenderingIntent: INTENT_PERCEPTUAL (nothing can change it: WcsSetDefaultRenderingIntent is a stub).
- WcsCreateIccProfile: NULL, ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER (every profile Wine opens is ICC; it was a raising stub).
- WcsOpenColorProfileW: the "no WCS support" FIXME only when CAMP/GMMP data is really given.
- GetColorProfileFromHandle: the NULL-buffer size query also sets ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER.
Kill switch: NEUTRON_DISABLE_WCS_PROFILES=1 (every Wcs* answers ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED again, the size queries behave
as before).

INFERRED (not measured): CPST_CUSTOM_WORKING_SPACE with a NULL device is treated like CPST_RGB_WORKING_SPACE (the other
working space); GetColorDirectoryW's short (non-NULL) buffer error is taken from GetStandardColorSpaceProfileW's.

Not covered, and what still differs from the Windows 11 measurement because of installed files: Windows ships and lists
WCS-format profiles (8, e.g. wsRGB.cdmp) and names D65.camp / Photo.gmmp as the device-independent CAMP / GMMP defaults;
Wine ships none and cannot open them (no WCS support), so it lists none and answers ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND there; profile
counts, list sizes and the sRGB profile's size (3144 vs 3024 bytes) depend on the installed files; the standard profile's
name keeps the lowercase "srgb color space profile.icm" that wine.inf installs (Windows: "sRGB Color Space Profile.icm").
Also: per-user association lists and WcsSet* (still stubs); Wine never fills ICM\mntr from the Linux side, so a display has
no default profile unless something associates one (the KDE/colord profile is not bridged) and Affinity uses sRGB through
the fallback, as Windows does for a display without a profile; EnumColorProfilesW keeps its "*icm" glob; the newer
ColorProfileGetDisplay* (advanced color) API. Affinity's Settings > Color combo boxes do not drop down under the lab's
synthetic input (affcolor on 11.10-183c; not chased, not tried by hand).

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-183c2 = 11.10-183rc + this mscms, lab prefix PgI-ac2, nested desk, +mscms trace):
- Affinity Log.txt (written fresh at each start), ColourProfileManager error lines: this build 0, 0 (g1, g2); kill switch
  on the same build 8, 8 (j1, j2), the same 8 lines as 11.10-183rc (affcolor: 8, 8). The only other error line
  ([DXCore] "Failed to get factory") is in every arm. The previous revision of this patch: 0, 0, 0 vs 8, 8, 8.
- +mscms on this build, per monitor: WcsGetDefaultColorProfileSize -> ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND (no association, as on
  Windows), GetStandardColorSpaceProfileW size query -> 138 bytes, second call, WcsOpenColorProfileW("srgb color space
  profile.icm") -> opened and read; WcsEnumColorProfiles = 2 profiles for both scopes (sRGB + a lab test profile
  NeutronLab1.icc in the color directory); no Wcs FIXME.
- Display profile pickup (a3, n=1): with NeutronLab1.icc associated to class mntr (the value AssociateColorProfileWithDevice
  writes) WcsGetDefaultColorProfile returns NeutronLab1.icc for both monitors, Affinity opens it, no fallback call, Log.txt
  0 errors; association removed after.
- Settings > Color opens (s3) with RGB "sRGB IEC61966-2.1", 32-bit RGB, CMYK, Greyscale, LAB profiles and rendering intent
  filled; Log.txt still 0 errors after.
- wcsprobe and wcsprobe2 on this build: every line the same as the Windows 11 measurement except the installed-file lines
  listed above. Same answers from the i386 build (32-bit probes). Kill switch: every Wcs* query ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED.
- Wine's own dlls/mscms/tests/profile.c (mingw build): 212 tests, 0 failures on this build, on its kill switch and on
  11.10-183rc.
- Adobe (affcolor's scan): Photoshop/LrC import the classic mscms calls, GetColorDirectoryW among them (now with the
  Windows size convention); Photoshop's ACE.dll looks WcsCreateIccProfile up by name, for WCS-format profiles (none in
  Wine's store; it was a raising stub before). No Adobe run on this build.

